## 4. Definition of Non-Commercial Use

"Non-Commercial Use" means use that is not primarily intended for or
directed toward commercial advantage, monetary compensation, revenue
generation, commercial exploitation, or the operation or development of
a commercial product or service.

Subject to the terms of this License, examples of permitted
Non-Commercial Use include:

- academic research;
- teaching and education;
- student projects;
- academic theses and dissertations;
- reproduction of published scientific results;
- personal study and experimentation;
- non-commercial benchmarking and evaluation; and
- research conducted by universities, non-profit research institutions,
  and public research organizations for non-commercial purposes.

The fact that an organization is a university, research institution,
government organization, or non-profit organization does not
automatically make every use non-commercial. The purpose and context of
the particular use must also be considered.

